From: pkgdemon <pkgdemonteam@gmail.com>
Subject: NextBSD: input devices from the IORegistry (IOHIDDevice entries)
Origin: NextBSD, nextbsd/nextbsd-displayserver-support#2 (kernel side:
 nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#331)
Forwarded: not-needed

The kernel publishes every /dev/input/eventN as an IOHIDDevice registry
entry. Enumerate those with IOServiceGetMatchingServices instead of
scanning devfs for input nodes, and build each evdev udev_device from the
entry's properties instead of the kern.evdev.input sysctls:

  DEVNAME, devnode, syspath  org.nextbsd.DevNode
  MAJOR, MINOR, DEVNUM       BSD Major / BSD Minor
  ID_INPUT, ID_INPUT_*       PrimaryUsagePage / PrimaryUsage
  ID_VENDOR_ID, ID_MODEL_ID  VendorID / ProductID
  ID_INTEGRATION             Transport
  parent (sysname = phys, or "uinput"): NAME and sysattr name from
  Product, PRODUCT from BusType/VendorID/ProductID/VersionNumber, UNIQ
  from SerialNumber; the same synthetic parent libudev-devd made.

A node with no entry, or whose usage maps to no udev type (switch-only),
is classified from the sysctls as before; without /dev/ioregistry devfs
is scanned as before. Links libIOKit, CoreFoundation and libdispatch
(nextbsd-userland, /usr/lib/system). udev-iokit.c also holds the IOKit
watch the monitor uses (next patch).

